/// Where every graph runs. Two independent tables, one per lane, both copied
/// from a source that already did the measuring.
///
/// **Core ML units are iOS's `ModelPlacement` tables, verbatim.** A day of
/// on-device measurement lives in those values and the rationale lives with
/// them in `FermentEngine/Sources/FermentEngine/Processors/*/`; the pins are
/// reproduced here rather than re-derived, so the Studio fleet starts from the
/// same baseline the shipping iOS app runs. Two deliberate divergences:
///
/// * `ChipGeneration` is **not** ported. iOS moves AutoShot, DFNet and the
///   GigaAM and Parakeet encoders off the ANE below chip 14 because the
///   A13/H12 compiler mauls their graphs; Studio is a desktop app tested on an
///   M3 (chip 17), so every gate would evaluate to the same branch. The machinery comes back if and when Studio
///   has to answer for an older Mac — until then a gate nobody can exercise is
///   a gate nobody can trust.
/// * Only families with a real `.mlmodelc` artifact carry units. iOS pins
///   DINOv2 to the ANE; Studio has no Core ML DINOv2 artifact at all (its
///   visual encoder is the ONNX master), so the pin has nowhere to land.
///
/// **ORT providers follow measured ship matrices**: `docs/provenance/016-report.md`
/// §4.1/§4.2 and the exporter's 2026-11-15 A4000 qualification for GLAP,
/// SigLIP 2 and MERT. Windows ML automatic NVIDIA selection was additionally
/// qualified on 2026-11-16 (see provenance/2026-11-16_windows-ml_report.md).
/// A family sits on [`OrtPlacement::WindowsMl`] only after
/// its exact bytes pass the independent golden corpus on that provider.
/// Unqualified families stay on CPU. `music_highlighter` and the DeepFilterNet
/// family are measured *failures* rather than gaps: CUDA corrupts the former's
/// ranking (fp16 attention, top chunk 5→9) and hard-fails the latter at the
/// cuDNN level on asymmetric-pad convolutions, and the locked ruling pins both
/// to CPU.
struct Pins {
    coreml: CoreMlComputeUnits,
    ort: OrtPlacement,
}

